# Git must not rewrite line endings anywhere in this repository, and on three
# files in particular it would be a reproducibility bug rather than a nuisance.
#
# `data/external/koplev_drug_mapping.csv` and `koplev_drug_targets.csv` are
# written by Python's `csv` module, which terminates lines with CRLF, and both
# are pinned by a SHA-256 recorded in `data/external/PROVENANCE_PHASE3*.json`.
# A checkout that normalised them to LF would produce a file whose digest no
# longer matches its own provenance record -- silently, on someone else's
# machine, in the one direction a provenance digest exists to catch.
# `tests/fixtures/koplev_tiny/drug_mapping.csv` is regenerated and byte-diffed
# by CI for the same reason.
#
# So: no automatic conversion, on anything.
* -text

# ...and `git diff --check` must stop reporting the CR of those CRLF line
# endings as trailing whitespace. It is not a typo to clean up; it is the byte
# the digest was taken over.
*.csv whitespace=-trailing-space

# Committed evidence. Diffing a 24 MB JSONL helps nobody, and GitHub should not
# try to render one.
*.jsonl -diff linguist-generated
results/**/*.csv -diff linguist-generated

# Generated documents are evidence too, but they are meant to be read.
docs/*.md linguist-documentation
